WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.190
Find, reach and qualify the right prospects.

2
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.590
This is the video for Module 2 of Client Acquisition Basics.

3
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:16.260
This module is the engine of client acquisition. First, you build a list of 30 real, researched prospects.

4
00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:21.870
Then you write short, personal messages that people actually reply to.

5
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.980
And you hold short qualifying calls that tell you quickly who is worth a proposal.

6
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:41.370
A prospect is not a category like 'schools'. It is a named business, a named contact, and one thing you noticed. Thirty researched prospects are worth more than three hundred copied numbers.

7
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:48.800
Start with 20 warm contacts who know you, then add businesses from Google Maps, social media and directories.

8
00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:55.390
In a simple sheet, write the business name and location, and the contact person and role.

9
00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.000
Note where you found them and how to reach them.

10
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:07.120
Write one specific observation, such as 'menu photos are blurry'. This is what makes your message personal.

11
00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:15.840
Then give a score. One point each for clear need, can pay, and a decider you can reach. Contact the 3s first.

12
00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:23.080
Only record business details the business itself made public, or that someone gave you with permission.

13
00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:29.650
Do not copy members' numbers from private WhatsApp groups to message them for business.

14
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:42.270
Keep your sheet private, and delete people who ask you to stop contacting you. The Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 expects personal data to be used fairly.

15
00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:50.710
And never add strangers to a broadcast list. WhatsApp can restrict accounts that many people block or report.

16
00:01:51.960 --> 00:02:04.590
A message like 'I do graphic design, let me know if you need anything' is easy to ignore, because it asks the reader to do the thinking. A good message has four parts, under about 100 words.

17
00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.890
A personal opening. Greet her by name, and say who referred you.

18
00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:16.810
One observation that shows you looked. For example, 'I saw your new branch opens next month.'

19
00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:23.500
A useful offer. Connect your service to her situation, with a result she cares about.

20
00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:33.410
And one small ask. Not 'can we sign a contract', but 'would a 10-minute call on Thursday work?' A small yes moves her into a conversation.

21
00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:45.540
For example, Chioma, a designer, first wrote: 'I do logos, flyers, menus and more. Contact me if you need anything.' It gives the owner no reason to reply.

22
00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:59.740
Her new message greets Mr Tamuno by name, notes that his menu photo is hard to read on a phone, explains that a clear menu saves staff time, and offers a quick mock-up with no obligation.

23
00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:05.920
Just 74 words. Send 2 to 3 messages like this each weekday, during working hours.

24
00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:15.400
When someone replies with interest, do not rush to send a price. Hold a short qualifying call first, using a checklist called BANT.

25
00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:22.600
Budget. Ask gently, 'Have you set aside a budget, or would it help if I shared typical ranges?'

26
00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.890
Authority. 'Apart from you, who else will be involved in deciding?'

27
00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:35.940
Need. 'What is happening now that made you interested?' Listen more than you talk, and write down her exact words.

28
00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:44.270
Timeline. 'When would you like this in place?' If you cannot tick at least need and authority, you are not ready to propose.

29
00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:55.910
For example, Halima learned that a school wanted more enquiries within 6 weeks, and that the administrator could approve a small trial himself. So she proposed the trial.

30
00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:03.120
Nurture when the need is real but the timing is months away. Send something useful now and then.

31
00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:14.330
And let go politely when there is no need or no way to pay. That is not failure. If the budget is small, offer a smaller scope instead of cutting your fee.

32
00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:20.780
So remember. Research before you write. Keep messages short with one small ask.

33
00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:29.990
On calls, the common mistakes are talking about yourself first, giving a firm price too early, and ending with 'I will get back to you' and no date.

34
00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:36.230
Now build your list, send your first 10 messages, and hold one qualifying call.

35
00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.520
Continue with the lessons below.
